      "message": "fix(post): write P0 on zero-dwell G86 in grblHAL and Tormach\n\nLinuxCNC's canned-cycle interpreter requires a non-negative P word on\nevery opening G86 block (after G80 or at cycle start), and grblHAL\nfollows that specification. Both posts previously gated P on\n`dwell > 0`, omitting P when the bore dwell was 0.\n\nEmit `\"P\" + secs(dwell)` whenever `g === \"G86\"` in `onCycle` for both\n`assets/posts/grblhal.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach.cps`, pin zero-dwell\nand positive-to-zero dwell transitions in `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs`,\nand update the `grblhal.nc` and `tormach.nc` bore goldens.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/2362-g86-zero-dwell.md\n\nFixes #2362",
